# This file specifies files that are *not* uploaded to Google Cloud
# using gcloud. It follows the same syntax as .gitignore, with the addition of
# "#!include" directives (which insert the entries of the given .gitignore-style
# file at that point).
#
# For more information, run:
#   $ gcloud topic gcloudignore
#
.gcloudignore
# If you would like to upload your .git directory, .gitignore file or files
# from your .gitignore file, remove the corresponding line
# below:
.git
.gitignore

node_modules

# Operator tooling, not function code. The search-token backfill is run by hand
# from a workstation (see cmd/backfill_search_tokens); uploading it with all 18
# function deploys is dead weight in every artifact.
cmd/backfill_search_tokens/

# test/cmd/ is the ONLY test directory excluded, and only because
# test/cmd/backfill_search_tokens_test.go imports
# com.loooans.app/cmd/backfill_search_tokens, which the line above removes.
# `go build ./...` skips _test.go files so the current buildpack survives it, but
# `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...`, a future buildpack, or anyone exercising the
# staged tree gets "no required module provides package
# com.loooans.app/cmd/backfill_search_tokens".
#
# The rest of test/ is deliberately still uploaded. It is dead weight, and that is
# the intended trade: an earlier version of this file excluded all of test/ and
# re-included test/fakes/ with a `!` negation, because the root go.mod carries
# `replace com.loooans.app/test/fakes => ./test/fakes` and a missing replacement
# directory breaks module resolution. `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload` resolved
# that negation correctly on a workstation — the file lists were byte-identical
# with and without it — but Cloud Build did not, and every one of the 18 functions
# failed to deploy with:
#   reading test/fakes/go.mod: no such file or directory
#
# So this file no longer relies on re-including a path under an excluded parent.
# Shipping a few unused test files is cheap; a deploy that cannot resolve modules
# is not.
test/cmd/

#!include:.gitignore
